Hello Everyone!

Wanted to let you know that the demo is finally live with a small update patch!

Demo 1.0.1 Update:
-[b]Added Shared Keyboard option[/b]. This will allow users to play using the same keyboard/mouse, even when using Remote Steam Play. Throwing the dice will become the press of a button in that situation. (this is valid for sharing same controller as well!);
-Wrapped some texts to fit in the screen on some languages;
-Pause Menu can show be exit by pressing ESC or Pause Button on the Controller;
-Sometime when using the controller DPAD and Thumbstick, the cursor might become misaligned. I've updated the code so now DPADs and Thumbstick use the same code;
-Ukrainian/French Localization Updates;
-[b]Fixed error when health keeps disappearing after battles[/b]. Now health is always shown, but you can toggle off if you wish during your turn;
-Added a [b]small text when changing turns[/b], to show what turn you are on (Starts at Turn 1);
-Reduced [b]timer for Dice to show the number (from 5s to 4s)[/b];
-Made [b]dice "collision" effect happens more often[/b];
-Added variable to your save file about selected language, so [b]you don't need to keep selecting the language every time you open the game![/b] (The Welcome Screen will still show up);

Submitting this game demo was a personal achievement for myself, so I'd love to hear from you! So if you liked the demo, please consider writing a review! 

Or alternatively you can [url=https://discord.com/invite/QbNXSmgCtJ]join our Discord[/url], where you can check updates, give feedback, suggestions etc...

Thanks and [b]Avante![/b]

Hello Everyone!

I wanted to inform that the Demo for the Early Access of Avante! Atlantis will be release on the 29/11/2024!

Initially, the demo will contain:

- [b]2-Player Games only[/b]. There will be no AI/Computer opponent at this stage;

- [b]Controller Only[/b] gameplay. I'm also working to see how I can implement keyboard gameplay with 2 local players;

- [b]Local Play and Remote Play Together only [/b]. Play via internet with other will come in a later update;

- Localization: Only [b]English[/b]. But I'll be working to add Portuguese-Brazil, Spanish, French and Japanese ASAP;

- 3 Maps;

- 3 Unit Types (Infantry, Bazooka and Tank);

- 2 ways of winning: Defeating all Units or Reaching the opponent HQ;

- Settings: Window Mode, Resolution, BGM/SFX/UI Sound Volumes;

- Accessibility: Color-blind Settings;

-----

This demo purpose is to bring the gameplay to be available to all and to get feedback. After couple of weeks, I pretend to release the Early Access version, in which I'll keep updating with new maps, units, gameplay, etc... as we progress. The demo will later be update to reflect new mechanics/graphics/gameplay.

I really hope everyone has a chance of playing Avante! Atlantis. 

Story Mode will come much later, but I have lots of things planned, so stay tuned!

Any feedback and comments are appreciated!

Thanks and [b]Avante![/b]

Hello everyone!

I'm Danilo, the solo-dev for Avante! Atlantis.

Thanks for all the amazing support that everyone gave me through the social medias.
This is finally a dream come true for me.

Now let's talk game.

For this updates, I'll try my best to keep updates here weekly. I have everything planned for this game so development should go smooth.

Soon we will have our first build of the game, which will feature the following things:
- 2 Local Multiplayer Only (aka Couch Co-op), which can be played with Remote Play Together;
- 3 Maps: 2 Plains and 1 Desert biome;
- 2 Teams: Red and Blue;
- Predefined Units on Maps (No spawning new units for now);
- Units: Basic Infantry, Mechanized Infantry, Tank, Supply Truck, and Truck
- Basic Settings (e.g.: Mouse Sensitivity, Screen size, etc..);
- Basic Tutorial before a match;
- Basic SFX and BGM;
- Basic Combat iteration;

This will be the first of many updates of the early access stage of Avante! Atlantis.

My goal is to test with you guys the basic gameplay and balancing of units/terrain and multiplayer.

As an extra, here is a couple of things I have planned for future updates:
- Air and Naval Units;
- New terrain tiles (water, river, canyon...);
- More maps;
- Online PvP (based on P2P connection for now);
- and more!

That will be for now! 

Here you can follow my on [url=https://bsky.app/profile/superdannynp.bsky.social]BlueSky[/url], where I post more informal updates:

Any feedback and comments are appreciated! 

Thanks and [b]Avante![/b]
